� 시뮬레이션 에너지 없이 재계산\n   - ARPDAU 재계산\n\n9. **UI/UX 개선** (UI/UX Guide):\n   - 컬러 팔레트를 파스텔/따뜻한 톤으로 변경:\n     Primary: #5B8EC9(하늘), #FFB347(따뜻한 골드), #8FD694(민트초록)\n     Accent: #FF6B6B(코랄핑크), #A78BDB(라벤더), #5C5C5C(텍스트)\n     Background: #FFF8F0(크림), #3D2B1F(갈색던전), #1E1E3A(밤보라)\n   - '왕의 칙령' 선택 UI 추가\n   - '발견의 서' UI 추가 (네비게이션에 📖 탭 추가)\n   - 에너지 바 UI 제거\n   - 사운드 디자인 섹션 추가:\n     BGM: 왕국(경쾌한 중세풍), 던전(긴장감 있지만 귀여운), 보스전(열정적)\n     SFX: 통통 튀는 느낌, 과장된 효과음\n     참고: Stardew Valley, Moonlighter 사운드 스타일\n\n10. **불필요한 항목 제거:**\n    - 길드 시스템 (Lv.12 해금) 제거\n    - 에너지 관련 모든 내용 제거\n    - 왕국 레벨 테이블에서 길드 행 제거 → 왕국 방문으로 교체\n\n**Instructions:**\n1. Read each of the 5 documents in docs/ folder\n2. Apply ALL relevant changes from above to each document\n3. Overwrite each file with the improved version\n4. Keep all existing good content that isn't being changed\n5. Maintain the same markdown formatting style\n6. Update the README.md to reflect new systems\n\nStart with 01-game-design-document.md, then 03-game-systems.md, then 05-monetization.md, then 04-ui-ux-guide.md, then README.md. Skip 02-tech-stack.md as it doesn't need changes.","Role":"Document Improver","TypeName":"unity-developer"},{"Model":"pro","Prompt":"Create the CORE FRAMEWORK scripts for the Mini Kingdom Unity project. These are foundational scripts that all other systems depend on.\n\nBase path: c:\\Users\\JCHJ\\Desktop\\Antigravity\\mini-kingdom\\Assets\\Scripts\\\n\nCreate these files:\n\n**1. Core/GameManager.cs**\n- Singleton MonoBehaviour\n- Manages GameState enum: MainMenu, Kingdom, DungeonSelect, InDungeon, Combat, LevelUp, RunResult, Pause\n- Events: OnGameStateChanged, OnRunStarted, OnRunEnded\n- Holds references to all major systems\n- DontDestroyOnLoad\n\n**2. Core/EventBus.cs**\n- Static generic event system\n- Subscribe<T>(Action<T>), Unsubscribe<T>(Action<T>), Publish<T>(T)\n- Thread-safe\n- Event types in separate file\n\n**3. Core/GameEvents.cs**\n- All game event structs:\n  - ResourceChangedEvent { ResourceType, OldAmount, NewAmount }\n  - BuildingBuiltEvent { BuildingData, Level }\n  - BuildingUpgradedEvent { BuildingData, OldLevel, NewLevel }\n  - DungeonEnteredEvent { DungeonData }\n  - RoomEnteredEvent { RoomType, RoomIndex }\n  - EnemyKilledEvent { EnemyData, Position }\n  - BossKilledEvent { EnemyData }\n  - PlayerLevelUpEvent { NewLevel, Choices[] }\n  - UpgradeChosenEvent { UpgradeData }\n  - SynergyActivatedEvent { SynergyType }\n  - PlayerDamagedEvent { Damage, RemainingHP }\n  - PlayerHealedEvent { Amount, CurrentHP }\n  - PerfectDodgeEvent { }\n  - RunCompletedEvent { Success, Stats }\n  - DailyBonusRunEvent { RunNumber, IsBonus }\n  - RoyalDecreeChosenEvent { DecreeType }\n  - DiscoveryUnlockedEvent { EntryType, EntryId }\n  - KingdomDefenseEvent { Success, Score }\n\n**4. Core/SaveManager.cs**\n- JSON-based local save/load\n- SaveData class with: KingdomData, PlayerData, InventoryData, ProgressData, SettingsData, DiscoveryBookData\n- Auto-save on important events\n- Backup system (keep last 3 saves)\n- Uses Application.persistentDataPath\n\n**5. Core/GameConfig.cs**\n- ScriptableObject with global game config\n- DailyBonusRunCount = 5, DailyBonusMultiplier = 1.5f\n- RunFailResourceRetainRate = 0.7f\n- MaxPlayerLevelPerRun = 15\n- PerfectDodgeSlowMoDuration = 0.5f\n- PerfectDodgeDamageMultiplier = 2.0f\n- KingdomVisitPerDay = 3\n- BaseResourceDrops, etc.\n\n**6. Utils/ObjectPool.cs**\n- Generic object pool: ObjectPool<T> where T : Component\n- Get(), Return(T), PreWarm(int count)\n- Auto-expand when pool is empty\n- OnGet, OnReturn callbacks\n\n**7. Utils/Extensions.cs**\n- Useful extension methods:\n  - List<T>.GetRandom(), List<T>.Shuffle()\n  - Transform.DestroyAllChildren()\n  - float.Remap(fromMin, fromMax, toMin, toMax)\n  - Vector2.RandomPointInCircle(radius)\n  - IEnumerable<T>.WeightedRandom(Func<T, float> weightSelector)\n  - Component.GetOrAddComponent<T>()\n\n**8. Utils/Singleton.cs**\n- Generic Singleton<T> MonoBehaviour base class\n- Thread-safe, DontDestroyOnLoad option\n- Protected virtual Awake()\n\n**9. Utils/WeightedRandomPicker.cs**\n- Generic weighted random selection\n- AddItem(T item, float weight)\n- Pick() returns randomly weighted item\n- PickMultiple(int count) for non-repeat picks\n\n**10. Core/DailyBonusSystem.cs**\n- Tracks daily run count\n- First 5 runs per day get 1.5x reward multiplier\n- Reset at 5 AM daily\n- Events: OnDailyBonusRunCompleted, OnDailyBonusExpired\n- Uses SaveManager to persist across sessions\n\n**11. Core/RoyalDecreeSystem.cs**\n- Daily system: 3 random decrees offered\n- Player picks 1, lasts all day until 5 AM reset\n- DecreeType enum: WoodDay(목재2배), WarriorDay(공격력+20%), MerchantDay(골드1.5배), ScholarDay(경험치+30%), BuilderDay(건설속도+50%), HealerDay(HP회복+30%), ExplorerDay(보물방확률2배), FortuneDay(드롭률+25%)\n- Active decree affects dungeon runs\n- Persisted in SaveManager\n\nMake sure all scripts compile together. Use proper namespaces, XML docs, and Korean comments for game logic.","Role":"Core Framework Developer","TypeName":"unity-developer"},{"Model":"pro","Prompt":"Create the DATA LAYER (ScriptableObject definitions) for the Mini Kingdom Unity project. These define all game data types.\n\nBase path: c:\\Users\\JCHJ\\Desktop\\Antigravity\\mini-kingdom\\Assets\\Scripts\\\n\n**Create these files:**\n\n**1. Data/ResourceType.cs**\n- Enum: Gold, Wood, Stone, Ore, Gem, ManaStone, Herb, Crown(premium)\n- With display name, icon sprite reference, color\n\n**2. Data/BuildingData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- buildingId, buildingName (Korean), description\n- BuildingCategory enum: Production, Military, Magic, Commerce, Social, Special\n- maxLevel = 5\n- Per-level data array: cost (ResourceCost[]), buildTime, dungeonEffect (DungeonBuff), kingdomEffect (string description)\n- DungeonBuff: buffType enum (StartWeaponTier, SkillSlot, FoodBuff, ShopDiscount, ExtraRevive, ExtraLevelUpChoice, AttackSpeedBonus, GemDropBonus, CompanionChance, BuildSlot), buffValue float\n- Sprite icon, Sprite buildingSprite (per level)\n- unlockKingdomLevel\n\n**3. Data/EnemyData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- enemyId, enemyName (Korean), description\n- EnemyGrade enum: Normal, Enhanced, Elite, Boss\n- Base stats: hp, atk, def, moveSpeed, attackSpeed, attackRange\n- Grade multipliers (auto-applied based on grade)\n- DamageType weakness, DamageType resistance\n- DamageType: Physical, Magic, Nature\n- AI behavior: EnemyBehavior enum (Melee_Chase, Melee_Rush, Ranged_Stationary, Ranged_Kite, Summoner, Boss_MultiPhase)\n- Loot table: LootEntry[] (ResourceType, minAmount, maxAmount, dropChance)\n- Boss-specific: BossPhase[] (hpThreshold, patternChanges, newAbilities)\n- Discovery book entry reference\n- Sprite, AnimatorController reference\n\n**4. Data/DungeonData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- dungeonId, dungeonName (Korean), description\n- DungeonTheme enum: Forest, Mine, Castle, Volcano, IceTemple, DimensionRift\n- unlockKingdomLevel\n- difficulty (1-5 stars)\n- roomCount range (min, max)\n- Primary resources: ResourceType[]\n- Enemy pool: EnemyData[]\n- Boss: EnemyData\n- Room type weights: Dictionary<RoomType, float>\n- RoomType enum: Combat, EliteCombat, Boss, Shop, Rest, Event, Treasure\n- Background sprite, BGM clip reference\n- Special mechanic description\n\n**5. Data/SkillData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- skillId, skillName (Korean), description\n- SkillType enum: Attack, Defense, Buff, Summon, Heal\n- DamageType damageType\n- cooldown, damageMultiplier, effectDuration, range\n- SkillTargeting enum: SingleEnemy, FrontCone, CircleAOE, AllEnemies, Self, AllAllies\n- Special effects: knockback, slow, stun, poison, burn, freeze\n- VFX prefab reference, SFX clip reference\n- Icon sprite\n- unlockBuildingId, unlockBuildingLevel\n\n**6. Data/EquipmentData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- equipmentId, equipmentName (Korean)\n- EquipmentSlot enum: Crown, Weapon, Shield, Armor, Boots, Ring, Necklace\n- EquipmentRarity enum: Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, Legendary\n- WeaponType enum (for weapons only): Sword, Dagger, Axe, Bow, Staff, SwordAndShield\n- Base stats: StatModifier[] (statType, value, isPercentage)\n- StatType enum: HP, ATK, DEF, SPD, CRT, CDMG, MOV, EVD\n- Additional options: StatModifier[] (count based on rarity: 0,1,2,3,3)\n- setId (for set bonuses, -1 if none)\n- Icon sprite\n- Lore description\n\n**7. Data/EquipmentSetData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- setId, setName (Korean)\n- SetBonus[] array: (requiredCount: 2/4/6, bonusDescription, StatModifier[], specialAbilityId)\n- Equipment IDs in this set\n\n**8. Data/UpgradeData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- upgradeId, upgradeName (Korean), description\n- UpgradeTier enum: Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, Legendary\n- Minimum player level to appear\n- UpgradeCategory enum: Attack, Defense, Speed, Magic, Special\n- Effects: StatModifier[]\n- Special effect description (for complex upgrades like 'chain lightning')\n- synergyCategory (for synergy system)\n- Icon, color\n\n**9. Data/SynergyData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- synergyId, synergyName (Korean), description\n- requiredCategory: UpgradeCategory\n- requiredCount: int (usually 3)\n- bonusEffects: StatModifier[]\n- downside: StatModifier[] (optional, e.g. 광전사: ATK+30% but DEF-10%)\n- Icon, color\n\n**10. Data/DiscoveryBookEntry.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- entryId, entryName\n- EntryCategory enum: Monster, Equipment, Building, NPC, Skill, Resource\n- description, lore\n- Sprite image\n- isDiscovered (runtime)\n- Milestone bonuses: DiscoveryMilestone[] (count, StatModifier[] bonus)\n\n**11. Data/RoyalDecreeData.cs** (ScriptableObject)\n- decreeId, decreeName (Korean), description\n- DecreeType enum matching the Core system\n- Icon, color\n- Effects description\n- Buff values\n\n**12. Data/StatModifier.cs** (regular class, not SO)\n- StatType statType\n- float value\n- bool isPercentage\n- ModifierSource source (Equipment, Building, Upgrade, Decree, Synergy, Discovery)\n- Apply(float baseValue) method\n\n**13. Data/LootTable.cs** (regular class)\n- LootEntry[] entries\n- Roll(float bonusMultiplier) → List<LootResult>\n- LootResult: ResourceType, int amount\n\nEnsure all ScriptableObjects have [CreateAssetMenu] attributes with proper menuName paths like 'MiniKingdom/Buildings/New Building'. All files should compile together.","Role":"Data Layer Developer","TypeName":"unity-developer"},{"Model":"pro","Prompt":"Create the GAMEPLAY SYSTEMS scripts for the Mini Kingdom Unity project. These implement combat, dungeon generation, kingdom building, and player/enemy logic.\n\nBase path: c:\\Users\\JCHJ\\Desktop\\Antigravity\\mini-kingdom\\Assets\\Scripts\\\n\nYou MUST use the following namespaces from other modules (they exist, don't redefine them):\n- MiniKingdom.Core (GameManager, EventBus, GameEvents, SaveManager, GameConfig, DailyBonusSystem, RoyalDecreeSystem, Singleton)\n- MiniKingdom.Data (all ScriptableObjects: BuildingData, EnemyData, DungeonData, SkillData, EquipmentData, UpgradeData, SynergyData, StatModifier, LootTable, ResourceType, DiscoveryBookEntry, RoyalDecreeData)\n- MiniKingdom.Utils (ObjectPool, Extensions, WeightedRandomPicker)\n\n**Create these files:**\n\n**1. Player/PlayerController.cs**\n- MonoBehaviour on the player character\n- Auto-movement toward nearest enemy (semi-auto)\n- Swipe detection for dodge roll (8-directional)\n- Perfect Dodge detection: if dodge initiated within 0.2s before enemy attack hits → PerfectDodge\n- PerfectDodge: Time.timeScale = 0.3f for 0.5s, next attack deals 2x damage, golden screen flash\n- Auto-attack at configured speed\n- Skill activation via skill slot buttons (2-3 slots)\n- Invincibility frames during dodge (0.3s)\n- Rigidbody2D movement\n\n**2. Player/PlayerStats.cs**\n- MonoBehaviour, attached to player\n- Base stats from GameConfig\n- StatModifier system: add/remove modifiers from various sources\n- CalculateFinalStat(StatType) → applies all modifiers (flat first, then percentage)\n- HP, MaxHP, ATK, DEF, SPD, CRT, CDMG, MOV, EVD\n- TakeDamage(float rawDamage, DamageType type)\n- Heal(float amount)\n- Events: OnStatsChanged, OnDamaged, OnHealed, OnDied\n- Apply equipment, building buffs, decree buffs, synergy buffs, upgrade buffs\n\n**3. Player/PlayerInventory.cs**\n- Manages equipped items (7 slots)\n- Manages resources (Dictionary<ResourceType, int>)\n- Equipment set bonus tracking\n- AddResource, RemoveResource, HasResource\n- Equip, Unequip item\n- Calculate and apply set bonuses\n- Persistent via SaveManager\n\n**4. Combat/CombatSystem.cs**\n- Singleton managing combat flow\n- Damage formula: baseDmg = ATK * skillMultiplier; defReduction = 100/(100+enemyDEF); finalDmg = baseDmg * defReduction * typeModifier * critMultiplier * Random(0.9,1.1)\n- DamageType modifier: weakness = 1.3f, resistance = 0.7f, neutral = 1.0f\n- Critical hit calculation\n- Damage number spawning (float text)\n- Kill tracking, XP distribution\n- Combo counter (consecutive hits without taking damage)\n\n**5. Combat/SkillSystem.cs**\n- Manages skill slots (2-3 based on Magic Tower level)\n- Skill cooldown tracking\n- Skill activation with targeting\n- VFX/SFX triggering\n- Skill unlock based on building levels\n\n**6. Combat/LevelUpSystem.cs**\n- Tracks XP and level (max 15 per run)\n- On level up: pause game, present 3 random upgrades from pool\n- Upgrade pool filtered by: current level (tier restrictions), not already chosen (unless stackable)\n- Synergy tracking: count upgrades per category\n- When category count reaches threshold → activate synergy bonus\n- Library building (왕립도서관) effect: 4 choices instead of 3\n\n**7. Enemy/EnemyController.cs**\n- MonoBehaviour for enemy behavior\n- Initialize from EnemyData\n- AI state machine: Idle, Chase, Attack, Retreat, Stunned, Dead\n- Behavior patterns based on EnemyBehavior enum\n- Attack patterns with wind-up time (for dodge timing)\n- Wind-up visual indicator (red flash/circle) to help players dodge\n- Drop loot on death\n- Publish EnemyKilledEvent\n\n**8. Enemy/EnemySpawner.cs**\n- Spawn enemies for a room based on DungeonData and room config\n- Wave spawning support (wave 1, wave 2...)\n- Spawn positioning (avoid player, spread out)\n- Elite/Boss special spawn effects\n- Room clear detection (all enemies dead)\n\n**9. Enemy/BossController.cs** (extends EnemyController)\n- Phase system: phase transitions at HP thresholds\n- Each phase can add new attack patterns, speed changes, minion summons\n- Phase transition cinematic (brief pause, effect, BGM change trigger)\n- HP bar with phase markers\n\n**10. Dungeon/DungeonGenerator.cs**\n- Procedural dungeon generation from DungeonData config\n- Room sequence: Entrance → [random rooms] → Boss\n- Guaranteed rest/shop at midpoint\n- Room type weighted random from DungeonData.roomWeights\n- Difficulty curve: enemies get stronger toward boss\n- 30% chance of branch paths (choice between 2 room types)\n- Output: List<RoomConfig> defining the dungeon layout\n\n**11. Dungeon/RoomManager.cs**\n- MonoBehaviour managing current room\n- Room lifecycle: Enter → Active → Clear → Reward → Exit\n- Room type handlers: CombatRoom, ShopRoom, RestRoom, EventRoom, TreasureRoom, BossRoom\n- Transition between rooms (door interaction)\n- Room clear rewards\n\n**12. Dungeon/DungeonRunManager.cs**\n- Manages entire dungeon run lifecycle\n- Run start: apply building buffs, decree buffs, daily bonus\n- Track run stats: rooms cleared, enemies killed, damage dealt/taken, resources collected\n- Run end: calculate final rewards (with multipliers), save stats\n- RunResult data class\n\n**13. Kingdom/BuildingManager.cs**\n- Manages all buildings in the kingdom\n- Build, upgrade, demolish buildings\n- Building placement on grid\n- Construction timer (real-time)\n- Calculate total building levels → kingdom level\n- Track dungeon buff aggregate from all buildings\n- Persist via SaveManager\n\n**14. Kingdom/ResourceManager.cs**\n- Singleton managing all resources\n- Add, Remove, Has, Get resource methods\n- Resource production from buildings (time-based)\n- Resource change events\n- Daily reset tracking\n- Persist via SaveManager\n\n**15. Kingdom/KingdomDefenseSystem.cs**\n- Weekly kingdom defense event (Wednesday)\n- Auto-calculate defense score from: building levels, resident count, wall level\n- Enemy wave difficulty scales with kingdom level\n- Result: Success (bonus resources) or Partial Fail (small resource loss)\n- Defense score = sum(building.defenseValue * building.level) + residentCount * 5\n\n**16. Kingdom/DiscoveryBookManager.cs**\n- Tracks all discovered entries (monsters, items, buildings, NPCs, skills, resources)\n- Unlock entry when first encountered\n- Calculate milestone bonuses (e.g., discover 10 monsters → ATK+2%)\n- Publish DiscoveryUnlockedEvent\n- Persist via SaveManager\n- Provide total discovery percentage\n\n**17. Items/LootManager.cs**\n- Process enemy drops using LootTable\n- Apply multipliers: daily bonus, decree, building bonuses\n- Spawn loot visuals (coins, resource icons floating toward player)\n- End-of-room loot summary\n- End-of-run loot calculation with fail retention (70%)\n\n**18. Items/EquipmentManager.cs**\n- Equipment crafting from recipe (resources + blueprint)\n- Equipment enhancement (+1 to +10)\n- Enhancement success rates: +1~5=100%, +6~8=70%, +9~10=50%\n- Failure: no destruction, just stays at current level (casual-friendly)\n- Set bonus calculation and application\n\nWrite complete implementations. Each file should be a self-contained, compilable C# script with proper Unity patterns.","Role":"Gameplay Systems Developer","TypeName":"unity-developer"},{"Model":"pro","Prompt":"Create the UI FRAMEWORK and screen scripts for the Mini Kingdom Unity project.\n\nBase path: c:\\Users\\JCHJ\\Desktop\\Antigravity\\mini-kingdom\\Assets\\Scripts\\\n\nYou MUST use the following namespaces from other modules (they exist, don't redefine them):\n- MiniKingdom.Core (GameManager, EventBus, GameEvents, SaveManager, GameConfig)\n- MiniKingdom.Data (all ScriptableObjects)\n- MiniKingdom.Utils (ObjectPool, Extensions)\n- MiniKingdom.Kingdom (BuildingManager, ResourceManager)\n- MiniKingdom.Combat (CombatSystem, LevelUpSystem)\n- MiniKingdom.Dungeon (DungeonRunManager)\n- MiniKingdom.Player (PlayerStats, PlayerInventory)\n- MiniKingdom.Items (EquipmentManager, LootManager)\n\n**Create these files:**\n\n**1. UI/Core/UIManager.cs**\n- Singleton managing all UI screens\n- Screen stack system (push/pop screens)\n- Show(screenType), Hide(screenType), Toggle(screenType)\n- Screen types: Kingdom, DungeonSelect, InDungeon_HUD, LevelUp, RunResult, Shop, Building, Inventory, DiscoveryBook, RoyalDecree, Settings, Pause, KingdomDefense\n- Manages transitions between screens (fade, slide)\n- Modal popup system (confirmation, info, reward)\n- ScreenBase abstract class all screens inherit from\n\n**2. UI/Core/ScreenBase.cs**\n- Abstract MonoBehaviour base class for all UI screens\n- Abstract methods: OnScreenShow(), OnScreenHide(), OnScreenUpdate()\n- Show/Hide animations (CanvasGroup alpha, scale bounce)\n- BackButton handling\n- Reference to UIManager\n\n**3. UI/Core/PopupManager.cs**\n- Show confirmation popup (title, message, confirm, cancel callbacks)\n- Show reward popup (list of rewards with animations)\n- Show info popup (title, message, close)\n- Show toast notification (brief message at top)\n- Queue popups if multiple triggered simultaneously\n\n**4. UI/Core/UIAnimations.cs**\n- Static utility class for UI animations (using DOTween-style API or Unity's built-in)\n- FadeIn/FadeOut (CanvasGroup)\n- ScaleBounce (transform scale 0→1.1→1.0)\n- SlideIn/SlideOut (from left/right/top/bottom)\n- PunchScale (quick scale pulse)\n- FloatNumber (damage/heal numbers floating up and fading)\n- ShakeTransform (screen shake)\n- CoinFlyTo (resource icons fly from source to resource counter)\n\n**5. UI/Screens/KingdomScreen.cs**\n- Main hub screen\n- Top bar: Kingdom level, resource counts (gold, wood, stone, etc.) with animated counters\n- Center: Kingdom view (scrollable, zoomable grid with buildings)\n- Bottom tab bar: Build, Explore, Residents, Shop, DiscoveryBook\n- Building tap → BuildingInfoPopup\n- Daily bonus remaining runs indicator\n- Active Royal Decree display\n- Construction progress indicators on buildings\n- Kingdom defense countdown (if upcoming)\n\n**6. UI/Screens/DungeonSelectScreen.cs**\n- List of available dungeons (scrollable cards)\n- Each card: dungeon name, difficulty stars, primary rewards, thumbnail\n- Difficulty sub-selection per dungeon (Normal, Hard, Hell)\n- Locked dungeons grayed out with unlock requirement\n- Current equipment/stats summary\n- Daily bonus runs remaining badge\n- Big 'Depart!' CTA button at bottom\n\n**7. UI/Screens/DungeonHUDScreen.cs**\n- In-dungeon overlay (always visible during gameplay)\n- Top: HP bar (animated), player level, pause button, speed toggle (x1/x2)\n- Mini-map or room progress indicator (dots showing current room position)\n- Bottom: Skill buttons (2-3) with cooldown radial fill\n- Combo counter (top-right, appears on consecutive hits)\n- Boss HP bar (appears during boss fights, shows phase markers)\n- Resource pickup counter (floating numbers)\n- Perfect Dodge indicator flash\n\n**8. UI/Screens/LevelUpScreen.cs**\n- Overlay popup when player levels up\n- 'Level Up!' title with star animation\n- 3 (or 4 with library) upgrade cards side by side\n- Each card: icon, name, description, stat changes, tier color border\n- Synergy hint at bottom ('공격 3개 선택 시 광전사 시너지!')\n- Tap card to select → confirmation animation → resume game\n- Timer: 15 seconds auto-select random if no choice (AFK protection)\n\n**9. UI/Screens/RunResultScreen.cs**\n- Shown after dungeon run ends (success or failure)\n- Success: '🎉 던전 클리어!' with confetti animation\n- Failure: '아쉽지만...' with softer tone (not punishing)\n- Reward list with count-up animation (gold coins, resources appearing one by one)\n- Daily bonus multiplier display (if applicable, 'x1.5 일일 보너스!')\n- Kingdom contribution bar (progress toward next building goal)\n- 'Watch Ad for x2' button (optional, non-intrusive)\n- Buttons: 'Return to Kingdom' / 'Try Again'\n- Run stats summary (rooms cleared, enemies killed, max combo, perfect dodges)\n\n**10. UI/Screens/RoyalDecreeScreen.cs**\n- Shown once daily (on first login or after 5 AM reset)\n- '오늘의 왕의 칙령' title\n- 3 decree cards with: icon, name, effect description, color theme\n- Cards have flip animation on appear\n- Select one → golden border highlight → confirm button\n- Active decree badge appears on kingdom screen\n\n**11. UI/Screens/DiscoveryBookScreen.cs**\n- Tab-based UI: Monsters, Equipment, Buildings, NPCs, Skills, Resources\n- Grid of icons (discovered = color, undiscovered = silhouette with '?')\n- Tap discovered entry → detail panel (name, image, lore, stats)\n- Overall completion percentage per category\n- Milestone rewards display (e.g., 'Monsters 10/30 → ATK+2% ✅')\n- Reward claim button for unclaimed milestones\n\n**12. UI/Screens/BuildingDetailScreen.cs**\n- Shows when tapping a building in kingdom\n- Building image (current level appearance)\n- Name, level, description\n- Current effects (dungeon buff, kingdom buff)\n- Upgrade button with cost display\n- Upgrade preview (next level effects)\n- Assigned resident info\n- Demolish option (with confirmation)\n\n**13. UI/Screens/SettingsScreen.cs**\n- Sound volume sliders (BGM, SFX)\n- Vibration toggle\n- Graphics quality (Low, Medium, High)\n- Language selection\n- Account linking (Google, Apple)\n- Push notification toggles\n- Font size (Small, Normal, Large)\n- Auto-battle toggle for cleared difficulties\n- Credits\n- Customer support link\n\n**14. UI/Components/ResourceBar.cs**\n- Reusable component showing resource icon + count\n- Animated count change (number rolls up/down)\n- Flash effect when resource gained/lost\n- Tap to show resource detail popup\n\n**15. UI/Components/SkillButton.cs**\n- Circular button with skill icon\n- Radial cooldown fill overlay\n- Pulse animation when ready\n- Tap to activate skill\n- Long-press for skill info tooltip\n- Locked state visual (if slot not yet unlocked)\n\n**16. UI/Components/FloatingText.cs**\n- Object-pooled floating text for damage/heal numbers\n- Different styles: damage (red), crit (large yellow), heal (green), resource (gold)\n- Float up + fade out animation\n- Slight random horizontal offset for visual variety\n\nWrite complete, compilable C# scripts. Use proper Unity UI patterns (Canvas, RectTransform, CanvasGroup). Include [SerializeField] for all inspector-assignable references.","Role":"UI Framework Developer","TypeName":"unity-developer"}],"toolAction":"Launching parallel development","toolSummary":"Parallel game development"}}]}
